4. Product experience: Basic and Advanced
4.1 Experience principles
Basic must be a complete, credible personal finance experience.
Advanced must offer depth, not merely a different color scheme or a longer navigation menu.
Both tiers use the same account, ledger, records, calculations, and security model.
Tier changes must not migrate, duplicate, delete, or reassign a user's financial data.
A feature hidden from Basic must also be blocked by the backend when the user is on Basic.
A Basic user's existing Advanced-created data must be preserved if they later switch to Basic.
No feature should be hidden purely because it is expensive to build or because the current UI is complicated. Prioritize removing specialist tools and simplifying complex workflows.
