4.5 Tier selection and switching
The user chooses Basic or Advanced during onboarding.
The choice is stored on the user account as an experience preference.
Both experiences are free.
The user can switch through Settings → Experience at any time.
Switching takes effect immediately after the server confirms the change.
The application should explain which features will become unavailable in Basic before switching down.
Advanced-created records remain stored and are never deleted by a tier change.
A Basic user switching to Advanced sees their existing data plus the newly available tools.
No payments, invoices, billing providers, paid subscriptions or payment webhooks are introduced.
Suggested user-facing language:

Choose how you want to manage your finances. Basic keeps everyday money management clear and simple. Advanced unlocks the complete TrueSpend toolkit. You can change your experience whenever you like.

