9. Onboarding and getting started
9.1 Experience goals
Explain what TrueSpend does without overwhelming new users.
Help the user choose the experience that matches their comfort and needs.
Avoid asking for sensitive financial information before it is necessary.
Make account setup skippable where possible.
Show an immediate, useful first dashboard.
Teach the application progressively, in context.
Let the user return to unfinished setup later.
9.2 Proposed onboarding sequence
Step	Screen	Required?	Purpose
1	Welcome to TrueSpend	No separate data requirement	Explain the product and privacy-first account model
2	Create account	Yes	Email, password, display name and optional invite code
3	Verify email	Yes before financial access	Confirm account ownership
4	Choose experience	Yes	Basic or Advanced, with a clear comparison
5	Personal preferences	Mostly optional	Country, currency, language, timezone and payday
