Index active verification/reset tokens by user and expiry.
Index invitations by token hash and status/expiry.
Index security events by (user_id, created_at DESC).
Ensure all user-owned foreign keys and child relationships are tenant-safe.
Inspect existing duplicate emails/usernames before adding unique constraints.
Use ordered, versioned migrations and a rollback/recovery procedure.
12.4 Transactional account creation
Account registration should be one database transaction:

Validate and normalize the registration payload.
Check or rely on database uniqueness constraints for identity conflicts.
Create the user in pending_verification.
Store the hashed verification token.
Create only safe default profile/preference records.
Optionally record a valid invitation redemption.
Commit.
Send the email through a reliable email delivery service.
Email delivery failure must not leave the database in an inconsistent state. Use an outbox/retry approach or a clearly recoverable resend flow.

12.5 Sensitive integration credentials
Audit Google Drive and other external-provider tokens.
Encrypt sensitive OAuth refresh/access tokens at rest using a managed encryption key.
Never return provider credentials through profile/settings APIs.
Support revocation and disconnect.
Rotate encryption keys through a documented migration strategy.
13. Frontend architecture
13.1 Authentication provider
Extend AuthContext or replace it with a focused authentication/session provider that supports:

